# Safety Herbarium — environment

# The core experience requires NO configuration and NO API keys. Clone, install,
# run, and every live source works: arXiv's Atom API and OpenAlex are keyless.
#
#     npm install
#     npm run dev
#
# Local development and the test suite use an embedded Postgres (PGlite), so there
# is nothing to set up. Everything below is for production only.

# --- REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION ------------------------------------------------
# A pooled Postgres connection string. On Vercel, install the Neon integration and
# this variable is injected for you. Without it, a production build refuses to
# start rather than silently using a store that vanishes on the next cold start.
DATABASE_URL=

# --- OPTIONAL --------------------------------------------------------------
# Public base URL of the deployment. Must be the public production alias with no
# trailing slash. Used for canonical URLs, OpenGraph metadata, the sitemap, the
# README badge and public/mcp.json. Falls back to the configured alias if unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://safety-herbarium.vercel.app

# Absolute path to the embedded PGlite data directory for local development.
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR=.pgdata

# --- LOCAL VERIFICATION ONLY ----------------------------------------------
# Lets `next build && next start` run without DATABASE_URL by re-enabling the
# embedded store. Never set this on a real deployment.
# HERBARIUM_ALLOW_EMBEDDED_STORE=1